[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m To solve the problem, we need to find the sum of all integer bases \( b > 9 \) for which \( 17_b \) is a divisor of \( 97_b \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m First, we convert the numbers from base \( b \) to base 10:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \( 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \( 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m We need \( b + 7 \) to divide \( 9b + 7 \). This can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k \cdot (b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m for some integer \( k \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m Rearranging this equation, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k \cdot b + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m For \( b \) to be an integer greater than 9, \( \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \) must be an integer. We denote \( d = 9 - k \), so the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ b = \frac{56}{d} - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m We need \( b > 9 \), which implies:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ \frac{56}{d} > 16 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[ d < 3.5 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m The positive divisors of 56 less than 3.5 are 1 and 2. Thus, we consider:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \( d = 1 \) gives \( b = 49 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \( d = 2 \) gives \( b = 21 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
