[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m To compute the sum of the positive divisors of \(9!\) that have units digit 1, we start by noting that \(9! = 362880\). The prime factorization of \(9!\) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(9!\) that end with the digit 1, i.e., divisors congruent to 1 modulo 10. These divisors must be coprime to 10 (i.e., not divisible by 2 or 5) because numbers ending in 1 cannot be even or end with 5.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m The divisors we consider are formed by the prime factors 3 and 7. These can be written as \(3^b \times 7^d\) where \(0 \leq b \leq 4\) and \(0 \leq d \leq 1\). We list all such divisors:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m For \(d = 0\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^0 \times 7^0 = 1\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^1 \times 7^0 = 3\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^2 \times 7^0 = 9\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^3 \times 7^0 = 27\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^4 \times 7^0 = 81\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m For \(d = 1\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^0 \times 7^1 = 7\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^1 \times 7^1 = 21\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^2 \times 7^1 = 63\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^3 \times 7^1 = 189\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(3^4 \times 7^1 = 567\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m Now, we check which of these divisors are congruent to 1 modulo 10:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(1 \mod 10 = 1\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(21 \mod 10 = 1\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m - \(81 \mod 10 = 1\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m Thus, the divisors are 1, 21, and 81. Summing these, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m \[1 + 21 + 81 = 103\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=468018)[0m Therefore, the sum of the positive divisors of \(9!\) that have units digit 1 is \(\boxed{103}\).
